IMPORT prelude

-- Long Service Leave Act 1987 (SA) -- the dates, in one small module. It uses only the built-in date functions
-- (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH, DATE_YEAR) and FLOOR, not the daydate library,
-- and defines no YMD.
--
-- The Act counts in completed years of service (s 5(7)), in months ("within two months", s 6(1)(i); "within 12 months
-- after the completion of an apprenticeship", s 6(3)), in years ("at least three years after the termination", s
-- 10(2)(c); "more than three years before the date of the application", s 13(4); "within three years after the date on
-- which the offence is alleged to have been committed", s 15(2)) and in days ("at least 60 days notice", s 7(3); "not
-- being less than 14 days", "within 14 days", s 12).
--
-- READING (fork F1 in NOTES.md; the text does not say): a period of months or years after a day ends on the same day of
-- the month that many months later (the day itself is not counted), or on that month's last day where it is shorter
-- (31 December plus 2 months is 28 or 29 February; 29 February 2024 plus 3 years is 28 February 2027).
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (the Act's current
-- version, 1.7.2017, as the register's unauthorised RTF). State of South Australia, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Long Service Leave Act 1987`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is on or before` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is before` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the first day` `to` `the second day` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the second day` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the first day`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `plus days` n MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` PLUS n)

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` a `and` b MEANS IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger of` a `and` b MEANS IF a AT LEAST b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days in month` m `of` y MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 12
    THEN 31
    ELSE DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (m PLUS 1) y) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 m y)

-- Fork F1: the same day of the month n months later, or that month's last day where it is shorter.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `plus months` n MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY (`the smaller of` (DATE_DAY `the day`) `and` (`the number of days in month` `the new month` `of` `the new year`)) `the new month` `the new year`
    WHERE
        `the month count` MEANS (DATE_YEAR `the day` TIMES 12) PLUS (DATE_MONTH `the day` MINUS 1) PLUS n
        `the new year`    MEANS FLOOR (`the month count` DIVIDED BY 12)
        `the new month`   MEANS (`the month count` MINUS (`the new year` TIMES 12)) PLUS 1

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `plus years` n MEANS `the day` `plus months` (n TIMES 12)

-- Fork F2: the number of whole years of service from a first day to a last day, both days counted: a year is complete
-- when the day after the last day reaches the anniversary of the first day. Service from 1 March 2015 to 28 February
-- 2025 is 10 completed years; to 27 February 2025 it is 9. From 29 February, the anniversary in a common year is 1 March.
GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the last day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the completed years from` `the first day` `to` `the last day` MEANS
    IF `the last day` `is before` `the first day`
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `the anniversary is reached`
         THEN `the difference in years`
         ELSE `the difference in years` MINUS 1
    WHERE
        `the day after` MEANS `the last day` `plus days` 1
        `the difference in years` MEANS DATE_YEAR `the day after` MINUS DATE_YEAR `the first day`
        `the anniversary is reached` MEANS
                (DATE_MONTH `the day after` GREATER THAN DATE_MONTH `the first day`)
            OR  (    (DATE_MONTH `the day after` EQUALS DATE_MONTH `the first day`)
                 AND (DATE_DAY `the day after` AT LEAST DATE_DAY `the first day`))
